+## iPhone (FF build, 2026-11-12)
+
+An iPhone 18 Pro log of the FF build (frame generation on, a 30 fps target, Wide view, render scale 0.6) ran at 0.87-0.92 of real time with the GPU at 30-35 ms a frame and frame generation stopping 17 times. Its causes, each fixed in the ff branch:
+
+- The game's upscaler chain ran on the GPU, 5-10 ms of compute a frame: `UPSCALER_SOURCE` matched `agl_ndsr.pck` only, so Ocarina's `agl_ndsr_vr` / `_vr_light` stages were not upscaler shaders and the fork's `upscaler_chain` key was missing. Now 59 upscaler shaders are named, the chain is skipped and MetalFX draws it (Mac: `first dispatch of b106afba1a18faa9_b drawn by MetalFX`). `dispatch_overlap on` came over from the fork with it.
+- About 1,700 render pipelines the fork's X17 list recorded in play were missing from the prewarm list, so about 270 draws a frame drew with pulling stand-ins while 384 demanded builds filled the pending table for minutes on the phone's single build lane (one serial queue for two performance cores). A refused build was looked up again at every draw: 50k instructions a draw against 18k. Now: two build lanes at least, a refused key keeps its stand-in for 250 ms without a lookup (`pso_refused_recent`), and the X17 rows are in `pso_manifest.tsv`.
+- Those rows would have made the phone's first start compile about 3,400 bases with a vertex layout before the title (the Mac's prepare step took 202 s on 10 workers): the bundled archive held pair bases only, and a base with a layout was never looked for in it. `pso_layouts.tsv` (3,409 rows, made by `pso_capture.py` from a `DM_PSO_CAPTURE` Mac run) puts them in the offline archive, and `layout_bases.tsv` beside it lets the host ask the bundle for them: the Mac's prepare step took 3,409 from a test archive and finished in 2.6 s.
+
+Current on an M5 Mac at a native 60 fps, render scale 0.6, the owner's save in Castle Town Market: frame p50 16.67 ms, p95 17-21 ms; GPU p50 about 14 ms (about 208 render passes, attachments 436 MB loaded and 349 MB stored a frame); the replay thread 9-12 ms of CPU a frame, about 30k instructions a draw at about 2,000 draws, spread over hashing, state replay, argument encoding and the Metal driver with no single hot spot. `DM_NVN_TBDR=1` cut the passes to 116 but took the frame to 40-60 ms and the footprint to 11.2 GB. Open: whether a native 60 holds on the phone in the Market (its GPU is smaller than the M5's; a lower render scale is the lever), and a wait of the replay thread on upload slots (`tex_zero_fill`, `up_begin`) when an area's new depth targets are made.
+
 ## Unused border corrections
 
 Specialize unused sampler border corrections away ([mechanism](../../../docs/reference/rendering.md#unused-border-corrections-retain-sample-registers)). No sampler of this game needs a twin (no "border colour … Metal lacks" line, the mask 0 in every draw of a profiled frame), so every draw takes the specialization and the picture does not change. Measured on a MacBook Air M4, docked at render scale 0.75 (1920×1080), whole GPU, a window, in the fixed view of Hyrule Field with the most grass (`still.sh`), with the 264 render-stage shaders of that scene that sample through the corrections rebuilt in the new form beside the chain `971e0669b443` image and a host of that chain:
@@ -134,6 +144,7 @@ Its 37 kernels that correct samples, NDSR's network among them, gave about 0.25
 
 - [Draw passes that wait for each other again while images share memory](../../../docs/reference/frame-rate.md#draw-passes-that-wait-for-each-other-again-while-images-share-memory): resolved, `draw_barriers game` was off whenever family heaps existed, and fragment-only barriers forced full ones; M1 Max gameplay frame 23.4 → 21.7 ms.
 - [A shader build's Python finishes one shader at a time](../../../docs/reference/shaders.md#a-shader-builds-python-finishes-one-shader-at-a-time): resolved, the whole Mac map's cold build took 58 minutes on an M3 Max with 4 to 5 of its 16 cores busy; 30 minutes with worker processes.
+- [Frame generation between held presents](../../../docs/reference/frame-rate.md#frame-generation-between-held-presents): at the 30 fps cap, MetalFX makes a frame between each two presents and the display link shows 60; on an iPhone 18 Pro 0-1 of 300 frames dropped.
 - [Reads past a uniform binding's size](../../../docs/reference/shaders.md#reads-past-a-uniform-bindings-size): open ([GitHub issue #2218](https://github.com/seedds/nxnative/issues/2218)), long white streaks from the horses at Lon Lon Ranch and from Link's slingshot, and flickering parts of the slingshot and of the ReDeads' faces, reported with the uniform read bound on. The bound now takes the size the driver gives the GPU, rounded up to 256 bytes; the game binds sizes that are not multiples of 256. Not reproduced here before or after (the slingshot at Link's house, the ReDeads of adult Castle Town), so the reporters' retest decides.
 - [The blend helper's output reference on iOS](../../../docs/reference/shaders.md#the-blend-helpers-output-reference-on-ios): resolved, 22,296 of 42,848 Mac shaders failed to compile on macOS 26 ([GitHub issue #2272](https://github.com/seedds/nxnative/issues/2272)); the Mac compile now names the host's minimum macOS.
 - [A NaN colour under a zero blend weight](../../../docs/reference/shaders.md#a-nan-colour-under-a-zero-blend-weight): resolved, white clouds over the ground mist between Kokiri Forest and Hyrule Field and over the ferns at the camera in Kokiri Forest ([issue #1839](https://github.com/seedds/nxnative/issues/1839)). The mist shader `5ad65c0eefd09c7f` writes NaN at alpha 0 where its layer has density 0; NVIDIA's blender, with the option NVN's driver sets, adds nothing there, Apple's stored the NaN.
