e has them for other builds, gets `fps_target 0`: without the stubs the host would present every vsync and the game would run at double speed. On a main with neither a frame step nor an engine limit the host writes, the host keeps the game's own present interval whatever `fps_target` or `DM_FPS_TARGET` says (`hle_fpslock.c` `dm_fps_lock_engine`), except with `present_interval display`, where the cap is the present interval alone: a game whose only limit is its present interval and that steps by the time that passed (Red Dead Redemption) |
