+- none seen on a game. An interrupt, a SIGTERM or a failed delete while the NSP script replaced one of its outputs (an extraction, the rewritten modules, the NROs, a DLC folder, a shader capture, the shader package) could leave that output half deleted at its real path, and a reuse check that looks for a few files (`extract`'s: `ExeFS/main`, `RomFS.img`, the RomFS marker) could take it for a finished output on the next run. → [Stopping a build while it replaced an output left that output half deleted](../reference/packing.md#stopping-a-build-while-it-replaced-an-output-left-that-output-half-deleted)
+- before running the NSP script, a player had to install the .NET SDK 10, and builds then failed in ways that were about .NET, not the game: a translator that finds no runtime of its architecture (GitHub issue #54, #248), a Homebrew runtime the apphosts cannot find, a dll tied to one architecture (#803), the entries below. GitHub issue #1853 asked for the tools to be rewritten in Python or Objective-C. → [Building needed .NET, and finding its runtime kept failing](../reference/packing.md#building-needed-net-and-finding-its-runtime-kept-failing)
