+## Memory and address space
+
+- on the Mac, a game crashes once its address regions pass the profile's alias region: at launch (Trails in the Sky 1st Chapter: `sig=11 addr=0x1` at `sdk+0x15576c`, after an 11.27 GB region at alias +1.00 GB) or a little later (Just Dance: a null allocation past 4.375 GB after about 40 s, then a crash at `main+0x639ab0`), though the build's address region check reports a larger reach. A provisional profile's red line `past the profile's … alias region, the iPhone layout` says the same. Tears of the Kingdom's long-session memory-shortage Blood Moon (`[game] MSF / R / Rf` after about 87 minutes at +2.25 of 2.38 GB, issue #639) may be this too: not confirmed by a long session, and a mark near the top alone is not exhaustion. → [The Mac's alias region is the Switch's 64 GB](../reference/memory.md#the-macs-alias-region-is-the-switchs-64-gb)
+- large resources silently skipped, later a null deref where the resource is used; also visible as `SetHeapSize` asking for much less than the pool. → [Partitioning the guest block between alias region, stacks and heap](../reference/memory.md#partitioning-the-guest-block-between-alias-region-stacks-and-heap)
+- an `nn::diag` abort with Result 0 under `nn::os::detail::ThreadManager::CreateThread` → `ThreadManagerImplByHorizon::MapAliasStack`, on some boots and not on others, with no `MapMemory refused` line. → [Thread stacks placed at random in the stack region](../reference/memory.md#thread-stacks-placed-at-random-in-the-stack-region)
+- `SetHeapSize OOM: req 0x600000 > cap 0`, followed by an SDK abort in `nninitStartup` on the first provisional boot. → [Provisional Unreal layout leaves no heap](../reference/memory.md#provisional-unreal-layout-leaves-no-heap)
+- `nnMain` returns right after `nv::InitializeGraphics`, with no error (Hyrule Warriors: Age of Calamity); `[mem] SetHeapSize … + modules … > app pool` (Monster Hunter Rise), `[mem] SetHeapSize … + modules 0x5c00000 > app pool` (Catherine: Full Body); `SetHeapSize` asks for almost the whole application pool and fails at boot (Metroid Dread: 0xc9400000, larger than the heap region); the memory pool for the game's 96 MB GPU heap has no storage (`MemoryPoolInitialize` red line), then a null read at `main+0x2eb954` (Catherine: Full Body); heap allocations fail late in a busy scene. → [Heap sized from the application pool less used memory](../reference/memory.md#heap-sized-from-the-application-pool-less-used-memory)
+- `SetHeapSize OOM: req 0xffffffffe0000000 > cap 0xd0000000`, followed by an abort when allocating the launcher NRO. → [Offline NRO copies are not additional guest memory](../reference/memory.md#offline-nro-copies-are-not-additional-guest-memory)
+- repeated `[RED] MapMemory refused (0xd401)` for a stack source inside a loaded NRO's writable data, then an abort in `MapAliasStack` / `CreateThread`. → [Thread stacks backed by active NRO data](../reference/memory.md#thread-stacks-backed-by-active-nro-data)
+- `SetHeapSize OOM: req 0x120000000 > cap 0xd0000000`, then `Break#1 reason=0` in `nninitStartup`, with a backtrace through `nn::os::SetMemoryHeapSize` (`sdk+0x967a4`). → [A heap request beyond the heap region returns ResultOutOfMemory](../reference/memory.md#a-heap-request-beyond-the-heap-region-returns-resultoutofmemory)
