+- a movie (or another picture the game converts each frame) does not show: the screen keeps the last 3D frame while the decoder delivers every picture. A pass dump shows a pass writing one serial and the composite sampling another serial of the same size, the two Metal formats `RGBA8Unorm` (70) and `RGBA8Unorm_sRGB` (71). → [Textures of an sRGB / linear pair over the same storage](../reference/rendering.md#textures-of-an-srgb--linear-pair-over-the-same-storage)
+- a clear of, or a format-converting copy into, a texture made without render-target use is declined. → [Render-target use added on demand](../reference/rendering.md#render-target-use-added-on-demand)
+- `CRASH sig=11 addr=0x794` in `-[AGXG16GFamilyRenderContext_mtlnext drawIndexedPrimitives:…]+0x50`, called from `draw_`, right after the log line `texture upgraded to allow format views` (Metal API validation reports nothing first). → [A texture upgrade while a draw binds its arguments ends the pass](../reference/rendering.md#a-texture-upgrade-while-a-draw-binds-its-arguments-ends-the-pass)
+- `render target is a compressed-format texture …`; the pass's draws did nothing (the attachment was left out), or the pipeline-descriptor validation aborts the process. → [Compressed textures as render targets through an uncompressed shadow](../reference/rendering.md#compressed-textures-as-render-targets-through-an-uncompressed-shadow)
+- on an iPhone before the A17 Pro, the game runs until its first BC texture, then `failed assertion 'Texture Descriptor Validation' … MTLTextureDescriptor has invalid pixelFormat (134).` (or another number from 130 to 153, Metal's BC formats; 134 is `BC3_RGBA`) and `CRASH sig=6`, the backtrace through `tex_mtl`, `tex_by_id` and `encode_args`. → [GPUs without BC textures are refused at start](../reference/rendering.md#gpus-without-bc-textures-are-refused-at-start)
+- the boot aborts in Metal's pipeline validation: `MTLPixelFormatDepth16Unorm is not color renderable`. → [A depth texture drawn through a colour view](../reference/rendering.md#a-depth-texture-drawn-through-a-colour-view)
+- a G-buffer target holds only scattered squares (a different order for each 32×32 tile). → [The same texture attached at two colour slots](../reference/rendering.md#the-same-texture-attached-at-two-colour-slots)
+- `no render target could get an MTLTexture` (the pass skipped). → [Passes with no render target](../reference/rendering.md#passes-with-no-render-target)
+- a black world: everything rendered through a 3D LUT built by layered draws comes out black (every plane went to plane 0); `DM_NVN_PASSDUMP` shows no `L` line. → [Layered passes for vertex shaders that write the layer](../reference/rendering.md#layered-passes-for-vertex-shaders-that-write-the-layer)
+- a frame-time spike every few frames (the Metal HUD's frame-time line jumps by several ms at a regular interval) while the scene stands still; `DM_NVN_GPUPROF` over consecutive frames shows the slow frame with about 130 more render passes, each one draw into a 64x64 to 8x8 face of a cube or array level, and the next pass starting late. → [Passes into other layers of one texture level run as one layered pass](../reference/rendering.md#passes-into-other-layers-of-one-texture-level-run-as-one-layered-pass)
+- a GPU-bound frame with many passes on the same targets, one after the other, each preceded by a compute encoder of one dispatch (`DM_NVN_GPUPROF`: `compute / copy after pass … dispatches 1` between render passes of the same size); about 4 ms of GPU idle a frame inside command buffers in Metal System Trace. → [Compute dispatches between the draws of a pass run ahead of it](../reference/rendering.md#compute-dispatches-between-the-draws-of-a-pass-run-ahead-of-it)
+- a scene drawn only in a small square in the top-left corner of a black screen; speckled and blocky patches; a full-screen overlay showing one tile; the texture dump right after the scene pass shows the picture only in the corner, and `DM_NVN_HILITE` on the scene's shaders lights only the corner. → [Clears of attachments larger than the render pass](../reference/rendering.md#clears-of-attachments-larger-than-the-render-pass)
+- a point light (a lantern, a lighter) lights only one side of the room with straight, sharp edges, and everything else around it is dark as if in shadow; a dump of the shadow cube (DM_CTL `texraw`, every face) shows face 0 drawn and faces 1-5 all zero; more generally, layers above the first of an array, cube or 3D target keep their old or zero content after a clear. → [Clears of layered render targets in a pass that is not layered](../reference/rendering.md#clears-of-layered-render-targets-in-a-pass-that-is-not-layered)
+- `texture clear case not implemented … mask 0x1`. → [A channel mask that covers every channel is a whole clear](../reference/rendering.md#a-channel-mask-that-covers-every-channel-is-a-whole-clear)
+- `texture clear case not implemented … mask 0x8` while entering a rendered scene. → [Texture clears with partial channel masks or regions](../reference/rendering.md#texture-clears-with-partial-channel-masks-or-regions)
+- red lines for unimplemented mid-pass, partial-mask and partial-scissor clears (the clears were dropped); `depth-stencil clear with a scissor or partial stencil mask, cleared whole` (logged once). → [Clears inside a pass, with a partial mask or a partial scissor](../reference/rendering.md#clears-inside-a-pass-with-a-partial-mask-or-a-partial-scissor)
+- a pass loads a whole depth/stencil target every frame only to clear it: Donkey Kong Bananza clears a 2880x1620 Depth32F-S8 target with stencil mask `0x1`, before any pass is open, and loads 22.8 MB a frame for it. → [A depth clear over the whole target with a partial stencil mask](../reference/rendering.md#a-depth-clear-over-the-whole-target-with-a-partial-stencil-mask)
+- a tile grid in Ultrahand and Recall highlights; an `EQUAL` depth test rejects fragments writing the same depth as a cleared Depth16 target. → [Depth16 load-clears match fragment writes](../reference/rendering.md#depth16-load-clears-match-fragment-writes)
+- solid magenta blocks, exactly (255, 0, 255), hard-edged and aligned to the 16-pixel grid (16×16, sometimes two stacked): Super Mario 3D World and Super Mario Odyssey showed them only on the iPhone; Captain Toad and Origami King on a Mac, Apple M6, Captain Toad in about half the frames of the opening course, moving with the falling leaves. On an RG11B10F target (no alpha) the blocks are pure black or neon green, (0, 252, 0), and flicker, sometimes only part of a tile: Super Mario Bros. Wonder on an Apple M6 and an M1, most visible on the speech bubbles of dialogue; or non-finite pixels that bloom spreads into green blobs (NieR:Automata on the Mac). A rendered cutscene alternates brightness every game frame, with blocky bands of light and shadow switching on and off: each lighting-zone bit flips every frame (Xenoblade Chronicles 3, a read-only image load). → [Same-pass feedback read through a snapshot](../reference/rendering.md#same-pass-feedback-read-through-a-snapshot)
+- a scene full of deferred decals runs far below its target where the same scene with `DM_NVN_FB_SNAP=0` holds it, and the log's `same-pass feedback sampling: snapshot #…` count climbs by hundreds a frame. Tears of the Kingdom's first shrine on an iPad Pro 11 (M5): GPU p50 58.8 ms, about 15 fps, about 284 snapshots a frame (seedds/nxnative#737); Breath of the Wild on the Great Plateau, camera toward the Temple of Time, on an iPad Pro 13 (M4): 60 → about 42 fps, about 45 one-draw passes more a frame on the 1920×1080 G-buffer. Splatoon Raiders in inked stages on a MacBook Air (M2): GPU p50 22–26 ms against 11–14 ms in the hub, a one-draw pass and a whole-map snapshot of its 6400×6400 ink map (80 MB) for each ink stamp (seedds/nxnative#1063). The `[nvn] same-pass feedback up to frame …` line (every 300 frames) gives the snapshots, reuses and tile reads per frame. → [Same-pass feedback read from the tile](../reference/rendering.md#same-pass-feedback-read-from-the-tile)
+- the `[nvn] residency set up to frame …` line (every 300 frames) shows hundreds to thousands of additions from `fb_snap`'s line in `nvn_mtl.m`, gigabytes of them, and as many removals, with the residency commits' time and the submit thread's kernel time up. Tears of the Kingdom on an iPhone 17 (1.4.2, seedds/nxnative#931): 1,500-1,600 additions of 2.4 MB textures every 300 frames, residency commits 250-600 ms every 300 frames against about 25 in an older build, kernel time on the submit thread 1-2 ms a frame against 0.2. → [Snapshot textures taken by format and size](../reference/rendering.md#snapshot-textures-taken-by-format-and-size)
+- a scene with many bindless decals runs well below its target with the GPU busy, and a pass dump (`DM_NVN_PASSDUMP`) shows long runs of one-draw passes on the same targets, each loading and storing every attachment. Fire Emblem Fortune's Weave's battle maps: 31 consecutive one-draw passes on four 1024×576 targets a frame, 126.5 passes and about 1.4 GB of attachment loads and stores a frame. → [Bindless shaders taken as depth readers](../reference/rendering.md#bindless-shaders-taken-as-depth-readers)
+- a game that reads textures through a pool runs slower than its draws explain, with passes of one draw each on the same targets. A pass dump (`DM_NVN_PASSDUMP`) shows `SetRenderTargets` going on in the open pass and the pass ending anyway. Ocarina of Time in Kokiri Forest: two frames of four had 219 passes, 127 of them on the 128x128 reflection probe's cube faces, and frame times of 15, 15, 18, 18.5 ms in a cycle. → [Pool shaders taken as depth readers](../reference/rendering.md#pool-shaders-taken-as-depth-readers)
+- blocks over the scene where an effect compares against the scene's depth, changing from frame to frame. Short screen-aligned dashes or blocks over rock and wall surfaces, light blue (the sky behind) or black, that stay on the same surfaces as the camera moves; how large and how many depends on the tree and the render size. Per-pass snapshots (`DM_NVN_TEXDUMP` with `DM_NVN_TEXSNAP`) show the surface drawn whole, then a later full-screen pass painting the blocks over it. Or light square blocks, 8×8 pixels, in the sky over distant hills and trees, where a soft-edged effect fades against the scene's depth. → [Depth sampled in the pass that writes it](../reference/rendering.md#depth-sampled-in-the-pass-that-writes-it)
+- NaN texels in the upper levels of a texture the game fills level by level (each level drawn from the one above), and from there NaN wherever the texture is read: black speckles in whole 2×2 quads, white blotches once bloom spreads them, and a dark frame from the eye adaptation. → [Mip-chain pass sampling the level it renders](../reference/rendering.md#mip-chain-pass-sampling-the-level-it-renders)
+- bloom wide and hard around bright edges: neon letters swell into fat, filled shapes. With `DM_NVN_FB_SNAP=0` they are thin again, but the white blotches of the entry above come back. → [Upsample pass reading the level above the one it renders](../reference/rendering.md#upsample-pass-reading-the-level-above-the-one-it-renders)
+- text a game renders into textures for the title and the menus comes out upside down, while the scene looks right. → [Lower-left window origin](../reference/rendering.md#lower-left-window-origin)
+- geometry appears inside out and almost black; a fullscreen indirect-lighting triangle is entirely culled even though its vertex data and polygon state match the game. → [Queue initialization captures the raster origin](../reference/rendering.md#queue-initialization-captures-the-raster-origin)
+- a pink window with every command buffer ignored while headless runs look right: the first presents fail on the display command buffer with `kIOGPUCommandBufferCallbackErrorPageFault`, and after a few of those macOS ignores every submission of the process ("Ignored (for causing prior/excessive GPU errors)"). → [The residency set committed before a present](../reference/rendering.md#the-residency-set-committed-before-a-present)
+- `kIOGPUCommandBufferCallbackErrorPageFault` or `kIOGPUCommandBufferCallbackErrorHang` on a command buffer, and nothing says which draw or dispatch caused it; `DM_RES_CHECK=1` reports no `missing residency`. → [Naming the shaders of a GPU fault](../reference/rendering.md#naming-the-shaders-of-a-gpu-fault)
+- with present snapshots on (`DM_PRESENT_SNAP`, the iOS launcher's **Frame buffering**), a frozen, corrupted picture from the first presents; the first error is already `kIOGPUCommandBufferCallbackErrorSubmissionsIgnored` ("Ignored (for causing prior/excessive GPU errors)") on the display command buffer, then on every upload, segment and submission command buffer, and `[RED] present snapshots: the previous copy into a ring slot did not finish within 2 s`. With snapshots off the same game runs. → [A present snapshot's copy needs the same residency commit](../reference/rendering.md#a-present-snapshots-copy-needs-the-same-residency-commit)
+- after a GPU hang or GPU page faults, every upload, segment, submission and display command buffer comes back `kIOGPUCommandBufferCallbackErrorSubmissionsIgnored` ("Ignored (for causing prior/excessive GPU errors)"). Nothing is drawn again while the game's sound and logic go on, until the game aborts itself (`game called nn::diag abort`, about 70 s later); in full screen, WindowServer froze for 40 s and its watchdog killed it. With the fix the log has `[RED] GPU access revoked: the … command buffer was ignored`, and a Mac app shows an alert and quits. → [A GPU whose access macOS revoked stops the game](../reference/rendering.md#a-gpu-whose-access-macos-revoked-stops-the-game)
+- an abort at the first present: `[RED] upload batches belong to the submit thread only: up_begin called on thread 'nvn-present-link'`, with `pkg_upload`, `tex_mtl` and `present_now` in the backtrace. → [A CPU-written window texture resolved where the present is queued](../reference/rendering.md#a-cpu-written-window-texture-resolved-where-the-present-is-queued)
+- a game that renders below the screen's resolution looks soft on a phone, in a large Mac window or on a 4K screen. → [The present upscales through MetalFX](../reference/rendering.md#the-present-upscales-through-metalfx)
+- in handheld mode the picture fills only two thirds of the screen's width and height, in the bottom-left corner (the top-left with the upper-left origin), the rest black. → [The NVN present crops by the vi layer crop](../reference/rendering.md#the-nvn-present-crops-by-the-vi-layer-crop)
+- a scene turns narrow, with black bars at its sides, while the swapchain or window textures keep their size; circles come out as tall ovals. The log has `vi::SetLayerCrop 0,0 1200x960` and `present upscaling: ... 1200x960 → 1800x1440` in a 2560x1440 window. → [A crop only picks texels; the picture has the layer's shape](../reference/rendering.md#a-crop-only-picks-texels-the-picture-has-the-layers-shape)
+- one-draw passes on one target, hundreds of times a frame, with the same attachments each time (a `DM_NVN_GPUPROF` frame: `load` and `store` of the whole target in every line); a low frame rate that follows the target's size. → [Setting the same targets again continues the pass](../reference/rendering.md#setting-the-same-targets-again-continues-the-pass)
+- a pass on a very large target costs about the same however little it draws; `DM_NVN_GPUPROF` shows time proportional to the target's area. → [A render area for passes on very large targets](../reference/rendering.md#a-render-area-for-passes-on-very-large-targets)
+- `[RED] NVN unimplemented function called: nvnCommandBufferShadingRateImagePalette`, or `nvnCommandBufferBindShadingRateImage` or `nvnCommandBufferSetShadingRatePaletteMode`, every frame. → [Variable rate shading ignored](../reference/rendering.md#variable-rate-shading-ignored)
+- angle-dependent character smearing, or vertex-only pipeline failures with `invalid depth/stencil pipeline formats 16843012/260`, although the pass began with valid `260/260` formats. → [Ten attachment records for eight colors and depth-stencil](../reference/rendering.md#ten-attachment-records-for-eight-colors-and-depth-stencil)
+- Metal aborts at pipeline creation: `depthAttachmentPixelFormat (MTLPixelFormatInvalid) and stencilAttachmentPixelFormat (MTLPixelFormatDepth32Float_Stencil8) must match`. → [Combined depth-stencil formats stay paired in passes and pipeline keys](../reference/rendering.md#combined-depth-stencil-formats-stay-paired-in-passes-and-pipeline-keys)
+- undefined values blended into attachments the fragment shader leaves alone. → [No writes to colour outputs the shader does not write](../reference/rendering.md#no-writes-to-colour-outputs-the-shader-does-not-write)
+- undefined values in the components of a target the fragment shader does not write: a NaN or garbage alpha (or G, B) that later passes, such as bloom, spread. → [No writes to colour components outside the shader's output map](../reference/rendering.md#no-writes-to-colour-components-outside-the-shaders-output-map)
+- foliage, hair and fences drawn as solid quads (the parts the texture leaves transparent filled with its colour or black), dissolve effects solid instead of breaking up; once per run `SetAlphaRef …: the host has no alpha test`. → [The alpha test through a library of its own](../reference/rendering.md#the-alpha-test-through-a-library-of-its-own)
+- data a game builds in a target by combining draws comes out wrong; in Xenoblade Chronicles 2 indoor lighting has hard-edged dark boxes (world-space boxes in perspective, darker with the time of day) and lighter translucent rectangles elsewhere; in Skyward Sword HD a brown cast covers the distance and near objects turn into dark silhouettes, coming and going with the camera. A pass dump shows `lo=7` (or any value other than 3) on the `D` lines of the draws that write the target. → [Logic operations through a library of its own](../reference/rendering.md#logic-operations-through-a-library-of-its-own)
+- `nvnBlendStateSetAdvancedMode 8` (SRC_OVER) logged and blended with the state's own functions. → [Advanced blend modes as Porter-Duff factors](../reference/rendering.md#advanced-blend-modes-as-porter-duff-factors)
+- striped lighting: black and white bands that follow depth on every lit surface, as if every pixel were in or out of shadow at random. → [Stencil-mode texture views read through `X32_Stencil8`](../reference/rendering.md#stencil-mode-texture-views-read-through-x32_stencil8)
+- a character drawn as a dithered silhouette inside a dithered square (DRAGON QUEST VII Reimagined's hero). → [Stencil-mode textures from the texture builder](../reference/rendering.md#stencil-mode-textures-from-the-texture-builder)
+- `[RED] NVN unimplemented function called: nvnCommandBufferSetProvokingVertexMode`, once. → [The provoking vertex is the first](../reference/rendering.md#the-provoking-vertex-is-the-first)
+- `[nvn] SetConservativeRasterEnable on: ignored by host for now`, followed by `[RED] NVN unimplemented function called: nvnCommandBufferSetConservativeRasterDilate`. → [Conservative rasterization remains unimplemented](../reference/rendering.md#conservative-rasterization-remains-unimplemented)
+- characters (skinned models) invisible or stretched into streaks while the level renders; `vertex attribute format … does not match shader input type …` for a remaining mismatch. → [Integer vertex inputs](../reference/rendering.md#integer-vertex-inputs)
+- red lines 89 and 96 (`vconv_bind`, the CPU conversion every draw); about a quarter of Age of Calamity's replay thread in battle. → [Shadow vertex inputs](../reference/rendering.md#shadow-vertex-inputs)
+- an unsigned iOS build reports `[RED] pulling library ... not usable (no library ...)` and its draws wait for pipelines, either with the profile's `pso_mtl4 on` or with **Metal 4 pipelines** and **Pipeline prebuild** turned on in the launcher for a game whose profile leaves `pso_mtl4` off. Then the prebuild ends at once as if finished (`pipeline prebuild done: 7495 pairs, 0 bases built, 0 already archived, 7495 left to the draws, 0 failed, 0.6 s`), and the shader image holds `_bp_left_out` instead of the `_bp.metallib` files. Or packaging with `IOS_PULL=1` fails with `SKIPS[@]: unbound variable`. → [Pulling vertex inputs](../reference/rendering.md#pulling-vertex-inputs)
+- a fullscreen post-process draw writes no color, then a later blur composite darkens scenery while the character remains visible. → [Float32 vertex padding through integer inputs](../reference/rendering.md#float32-vertex-padding-through-integer-inputs)
+- `Vertex attribute m_36(5) of type uint4 cannot be read using MTLAttributeFormatHalf2` (draws dropped: black silhouettes); UVs collapse onto one texel (flat tan characters); vertices far out of view (negative 16-bit values widened with zeros). → [CPU conversion of vertex attributes the input type cannot take](../reference/rendering.md#cpu-conversion-of-vertex-attributes-the-input-type-cannot-take)
+- `[RED] BindVertexAttribState n=17`, tens of thousands of times, and a scene that draws wrong or not at all: the bind was refused, so the draws kept the previous layout. → [More than 16 vertex attributes](../reference/rendering.md#more-than-16-vertex-attributes)
+- `vertex attribute format … not mapped` (printed once). → [Vertex formats Metal lacks](../reference/rendering.md#vertex-formats-metal-lacks)
+- `[RED] vertex attribute conversion: a range of 915138 vertices exceeds the per-frame staging (format 0x14)` and geometry stretched into streaks from the picture's centre (a stadium's stands and roof), while the pitch, the HUD and the characters draw right. → [Long vertex ranges in the CPU conversion](../reference/rendering.md#long-vertex-ranges-in-the-cpu-conversion)
+- the `vertex conversion:` line reports millions of vertices per submission and the submitting thread's translation takes most of a frame: 7.65 million vertices, 122 MB written every frame, 26.8 ms on an M4 (about 37 fps) in the stadium above, as PR #1727 measured. → [Kept vertex conversions](../reference/rendering.md#kept-vertex-conversions)
+- `[RED] BindVertexBuffers first=16 n=1` … `first=31`, thousands of times a run and no visible fault. → [Null vertex buffers bound past stream 15](../reference/rendering.md#null-vertex-buffers-bound-past-stream-15)
+- the assertion `buffer index (31) must be < 31`. → [Vertex streams 14 and 15 at Metal slots 14 and 15](../reference/rendering.md#vertex-streams-14-and-15-at-metal-slots-14-and-15)
+- Scaleform fills come out as solid white or light grey sheets over the whole screen, hard-edged triangles and bands, and the menu text is missing (a language list or a title screen that is all white behind its button prompt). → [Vertex streams at addresses that are not 4-byte aligned](../reference/rendering.md#vertex-streams-at-addresses-that-are-not-4-byte-aligned)
+- hard-edged translucent slabs and triangles over the scene that move with the camera, where a full-screen pass blends an effect in (Super Mario Odyssey: white wedges through the Cascade Kingdom's waterfall mist, one edge through the centre of the screen). → [Vertex fetches past a stream's bound size](../reference/rendering.md#vertex-fetches-past-a-streams-bound-size)
+- `[RED] vertex stream N's buffer 0x… is in no memory pool; draw skipped` (`; its attributes read zeros` for a pulling pipeline, `; a geometry capture reads the buffer bound before` for one). Before the line existed: a draw whose vertices came from an earlier draw's buffer, with nothing in the log. → [A vertex stream in no memory pool](../reference/rendering.md#a-vertex-stream-in-no-memory-pool)
+- scenes and characters black, only foliage, light shafts and the HUD drawn; pass dumps full of `Z … draw skipped: no program bound`. → [Programs bound per stage](../reference/rendering.md#programs-bound-per-stage)
+- a draw disabled by `SetRenderEnable(false)` executes after an event or fence, or a conditional clear erases a target whose preceding timestamp report should make it skip. → [Conditional rendering survives queue continuations](../reference/rendering.md#conditional-rendering-survives-queue-continuations)
+- `[RED] failed to create render pipeline (vertex 790573a52b9c5053_b fragment f39fb42850f50ecd_b): Fragment input(s) user(locn0),user(locn1) … not written by vertex shader`, once on entering the first investigation; `texture type mismatch: shader declares a cube, texture is 2D` (a pixel shader run with another pair's bindings). → [Composite program taken again after a replay state restore](../reference/rendering.md#composite-program-taken-again-after-a-replay-state-restore)
+- `no program bound before the draw`, `program has no vertex shader` (a draw after a dispatch is dropped); `the dispatched program has no compute shader` (a dispatch after a graphics bind). → [Compute programs bound apart from graphics programs](../reference/rendering.md#compute-programs-bound-apart-from-graphics-programs)
+- a red line: the 8-bit index buffer had GPU-side writes in the submission (indices read stale). → [8-bit indices widened on the GPU after a write in the same submission](../reference/rendering.md#8-bit-indices-widened-on-the-gpu-after-a-write-in-the-same-submission)
+- indirect draws whose record the GPU writes earlier in the frame cannot be read on the CPU at replay; GPU-driven effects drawn as indirect quads, which Metal has no primitive for. → [Indirect draws and dispatches read by the GPU](../reference/rendering.md#indirect-draws-and-dispatches-read-by-the-gpu)
+- an empty G-buffer pass (the title screen showed only the UI); later, the submitting thread waiting for the GPU before each such draw (36–54 fps in Kamura Village on an iPhone). MIO also reported missing level geometry with maxima of 4,594 and 8,192 draws. → [Indirect-count multi-draws](../reference/rendering.md#indirect-count-multi-draws)
+- a hitch of a second or more as a level opens: a few frames of 330–540 ms whose submission takes 2–3 times its CPU time, and the wait ledger (`DM_NVN_WAITS=1`) shows thousands of indirect-count multi-draw waits for those frames only. → [CPU reads after a drain wait only for later writes](../reference/rendering.md#cpu-reads-after-a-drain-wait-only-for-later-writes)
+- a black screen while the frame loop runs at full rate, with `[RED] NVN unimplemented function called: nvnCommandBufferDrawTexture`; once drawn, the picture alternates frame by frame between the right image and another texture's (a solid colour, a still image). → [`nvnCommandBufferDrawTexture`](../reference/rendering.md#nvncommandbufferdrawtexture)
+- the HUD and sky render but the battle's characters and terrain are absent; the replay logs `draw skipped: rasterizer discard` between model draws. → [Rasterizer discard preserves vertex storage writes](../reference/rendering.md#rasterizer-discard-preserves-vertex-storage-writes)
+- exploding meshes and displaced model parts after vertex-only work; native post-vertex captures can contain valid positions for some meshes while other palettes are incorrect. → [Primitive barriers order vertex storage writes](../reference/rendering.md#primitive-barriers-order-vertex-storage-writes)
+- a character's mesh stretched for one frame into a long wedge or sheet that reaches another character, and other characters missing in that frame; intermittent (about one frame in a hundred near a group of characters). A pass dump shows `barrier bits 0x1 (render pass open)` before vertex-only draws (`fs=-`, `discard=1`) that bind a storage buffer `rw` which the draws before them read `ro`. → [Ordering barriers before a draw that writes](../reference/rendering.md#ordering-barriers-before-a-draw-that-writes)
+- characters collapsed into one thin spike (vertex streams read from feedback buffers that were never written); a character covered by a solid box while it moves (its fur shells pulled toward lagged positions that were never written); a pass dump shows draws with a vertex shader and no fragment shader (`fs=-`) before the draws that read them, and `Y tf begin … written 0/0/0/0` with no `T … tf capture` line. → [Transform feedback captured by a vertex entry point](../reference/rendering.md#transform-feedback-captured-by-a-vertex-entry-point)
+- a scene drawn with a geometry shader per mesh runs at 5 to 15 fps on the Mac, with the submitting thread or the GPU taking most of the frame. → [Geometry-shader draws encoded a run at a time](../reference/rendering.md#geometry-shader-draws-encoded-a-run-at-a-time)
+- `SIGSEGV` in `-[AGXG18GFamilyComputeContext_mtlnext performEndEncoding]` (from `rp_begin_ex_`, or in its `dealloc` on the encoding thread); Metal validation (`MTL_DEBUG_LAYER=1 MTL_DEBUG_LAYER_ERROR_MODE=nslog`) names it: "Command buffer already has an open command encoder". → [Helper encoders end the open copy encoder first](../reference/rendering.md#helper-encoders-end-the-open-copy-encoder-first)
