+- `failed to create render pipeline … output of type float4 is not compatible with a MTLPixelFormatR32Uint color attachment` (or `MTLPixelFormatRGBA16Uint`); every draw into the target skipped. → [Integer entry points for integer colour outputs](../reference/shaders.md#integer-entry-points-for-integer-colour-outputs)
+- a deferred scene with part of its materials unlit or black: grass, ground and trees dark while wood and characters look right, whole areas of a map black. There may be no red line. A texture dump shows an integer G-buffer target (`fmt=73`, RGBA8Uint) holding only zeros, and the lighting pass reads it. Since this entry, `[RED] shader … writes colour target …, an integer format, as a float`. → [Integer outputs told from float bits](../reference/shaders.md#integer-outputs-told-from-float-bits)
+- `failed to create render pipeline … Cannot convert attribute …`; draws missing (a pipeline that fails to build). → [Integer-typed vertex inputs fed normalized formats](../reference/shaders.md#integer-typed-vertex-inputs-fed-normalized-formats)
+- outdoors the whole screen blurred (depth of field out of focus everywhere). → [Depth mode near = 0 needs the per-mode entry points](../reference/shaders.md#depth-mode-near--0-needs-the-per-mode-entry-points)
+- `SPIRV-Cross threw an exception: Subgroup builtins are not available in this type of function`. → [Subgroup operations rewritten for a one-lane subgroup](../reference/shaders.md#subgroup-operations-rewritten-for-a-one-lane-subgroup)
+- the tone mapper read an empty LUT and the screen came out a flat blue. → [Geometry shaders that only pick the layer](../reference/shaders.md#geometry-shaders-that-only-pick-the-layer)
+- `[RED] NVN unimplemented function called: nvnCommandBufferDrawMeshTasks`, and a build that fails with `Ampere instruction 927 ... is not implemented` in shaders the map calls vertex or domain; what they draw is missing. → [NVN2 task and mesh shaders](../reference/shaders.md#nvn2-task-and-mesh-shaders)
+- large flat panels in front of the sky, the clouds behind them blinking at times, in some places and not others. In a `DM_NVN_PASSDUMP_ALL` dump every task and mesh shader's storage buffer shows as `st3` / `st4 sbufp reg6` or `reg7` `dummy addr=0 size=0`, though the game binds buffers for those stages. → [Task and mesh draws reading the dummy buffer](../reference/shaders.md#task-and-mesh-draws-reading-the-dummy-buffer)
+- a game with task and mesh shaders runs at a lower internal resolution than it could, or below its frame rate, and the GPU time sits in the pass that draws its mesh work (a render pass's start stamp is written after its vertex stage, where Metal runs the object and mesh stages, so in a `DM_NVN_GPUPROF` profile the mesh work shows as the gap before that pass or as its length). `DM_NVN_SKIP_MESH=1` (diagnostic: every task and mesh draw dropped, the picture wrong) takes most of that time away. → [Stage memory byte stores through a compare-and-swap loop](../reference/shaders.md#stage-memory-byte-stores-through-a-compare-and-swap-loop)
+- a geometry shader fails to compile with `unknown main0_out`: SPIRV-Cross writes `unknown main0_out main0()` for the geometry stage, and the shader does not build. → [Geometry shaders with no Metal stage](../reference/shaders.md#geometry-shaders-with-no-metal-stage)
+- the models a passthrough geometry shader draws are missing: its own draw (a depth prepass) shows nothing, and so do the draws that test against that depth for equality. Before the shader loaded at all, the same models showed as black silhouettes. → [Passthrough geometry shaders](../reference/shaders.md#passthrough-geometry-shaders)
+- `[geometry failed]  missing geometry topology buffer` in the build, then `[RED] shader … (geometry) failed to load` and those draws skipped. → [The topology table passed to a helper function](../reference/shaders.md#the-topology-table-passed-to-a-helper-function)
+- the host's memory watchdog closes the game (at 28.3 GB on Kirby Air Riders, whose Switch 2 has 9 GB), with the Metal heap full of frame arena blocks of 36 or 72 MB; it comes on quickly in a scene full of ribbons. → [A captured draw's vertex IDs far apart](../reference/shaders.md#a-captured-draws-vertex-ids-far-apart)
+- geometry reader compilation fails with undeclared `gl_BuiltIn_5253` and a scalar `.elements` access. Compiling only the compute kernel also leaves native passthrough geometry without emitted vertices. → [Geometry passthrough and viewport masks in compute](../reference/shaders.md#geometry-passthrough-and-viewport-masks-in-compute)
+- sorting repeated mesh indices consumes much of the render thread's CPU time. → [Geometry capture indices deduplicated with a bounded bitset](../reference/shaders.md#geometry-capture-indices-deduplicated-with-a-bounded-bitset)
+- later geometry uses stale shader-written data or appears in the earlier draw's position when draws are combined into a geometry run. → [Geometry runs retain external buffer dependencies](../reference/shaders.md#geometry-runs-retain-external-buffer-dependencies)
+- the CPU spends substantial replay time checking dependencies among geometry jobs that share many read-only buffers. → [Geometry dependency checks skip read-only pairs](../reference/shaders.md#geometry-dependency-checks-skip-read-only-pairs)
+- a game whose frames are mostly geometry-shader draws stays GPU-bound by attachment traffic: a `DM_NVN_GPUPROF` frame shows hundreds of two-draw render passes (each geometry draw, then the reopened pass of its raster) and gigabytes of attachment loads and stores, and no `geometry hoist` line ever appears in the log. → [An empty vertex stream kept every geometry draw out of a run](../reference/shaders.md#an-empty-vertex-stream-kept-every-geometry-draw-out-of-a-run)
+- geometry-heavy rendering spends substantial GPU time compacting the geometry shader's emitted indices. → [Parallel geometry index compaction](../reference/shaders.md#parallel-geometry-index-compaction)
+- the geometry kernel compiles, but its `_bgv.metal` vertex reader fails with `use of undeclared identifier 'gl_BuiltIn_5253'` and `member reference base type 'int' is not a structure or union`. → [Geometry reader viewport masks](../reference/shaders.md#geometry-reader-viewport-masks)
+- a passthrough geometry kernel writes beyond its vertex and raw-index scratch regions, and compaction reads the wrong groups; corruption can reach the following primitive-map buffers without a red diagnostic. → [Passthrough geometry output bounds follow input topology](../reference/shaders.md#passthrough-geometry-output-bounds-follow-input-topology)
+- a geometry kernel compiles and runs its storage-buffer side effects, but contains no `geometry_vb_output` binding and fills its index stream with restart markers; its following raster pass draws no geometry. → [Passthrough geometry kernels lose raster vertices](../reference/shaders.md#passthrough-geometry-kernels-lose-raster-vertices)
+- geometry-heavy frames have a large submission wall/CPU gap despite short GPU execution; stack samples spend most of the main thread in `geo_draw` → `mdi_wait` → shared-event wait, with index sorting another substantial cost. → [Geometry capture waits for every indexed draw](../reference/shaders.md#geometry-capture-waits-for-every-indexed-draw)
+- geometry-heavy frames remain GPU-bound after CPU readback waits are removed; encoder timestamps attribute most compaction time to the offset scan rather than the geometry shader or index writes. → [Geometry compaction serial prefix scan](../reference/shaders.md#geometry-compaction-serial-prefix-scan)
+- `[RED] geometry draw needs 261 MiB of scratch, above the 256 MiB bound` (or `exceeds the capture or invocation bound`); the draw is skipped. → [Geometry draws above the capture scratch bound](../reference/shaders.md#geometry-draws-above-the-capture-scratch-bound)
+- a geometry shader that reads `PrimitiveID` repeats its visibility decisions or storage addresses after a large draw is split into compute dispatches. → [Split geometry primitive IDs](../reference/shaders.md#split-geometry-primitive-ids)
+- a large geometry draw crashes in `geo_split` / `memcpy` while reading indices, sometimes preceded by `geometry draw exceeds the capture or invocation bound` for an unexpectedly small child draw. → [Recursive geometry splits retain their original draw range](../reference/shaders.md#recursive-geometry-splits-retain-their-original-draw-range)
+- geometry draws with transform feedback report `geometry draw cannot capture this pipeline` and write no feedback records after the geometry-job integration. → [Geometry jobs preserve transform-feedback replay](../reference/shaders.md#geometry-jobs-preserve-transform-feedback-replay)
+- geometry-heavy frames are GPU-bound on the emulation itself. A `DM_NVN_GPUPROF` frame shows, for every geometry draw, a capture pass (`0x0 0c`), a compute encoder and a one-draw reopening of the game's pass, with most of the frame's GPU time in the first two. → [Passthrough geometry shaders drawn by the vertex shader](../reference/shaders.md#passthrough-geometry-shaders-drawn-by-the-vertex-shader)
+- a pale blue wash over every 3D scene with atmosphere; the HUD is clean, and the albedo and normal targets are right. A 3D table (`texraw`) has data in plane 0 only, and the pass that fills it has no `L … layered pass` line and draws with `gs=-`. → [A passthrough geometry shader that writes the layer](../reference/shaders.md#a-passthrough-geometry-shader-that-writes-the-layer)
+- a passthrough geometry shader that uses `PrimitiveID` makes different visibility decisions or storage writes after the first 32 triangles when composed into a mesh shader. → [Mesh geometry primitive IDs restart per group](../reference/shaders.md#mesh-geometry-primitive-ids-restart-per-group)
+- after a pair is added to `geo_mesh.tsv`, `[RED] geometry mesh pipeline: ... Total mesh size (37248) exceeds the maximum mesh size allowed (32768)`, and the frames that draw the pair get much slower than on the compute path (Donkey Kong Bananza: translation from about 10 to 22–31 ms a frame). → [Mesh geometry groups sized to the vertex output](../reference/shaders.md#mesh-geometry-groups-sized-to-the-vertex-output)
+- a depth prepass of many small geometry-shader draws, drawn as mesh draws, leaves the GPU nearly idle: the per-pass profile (`DM_NVN_GPUPROF`) shows an idle gap before the pass that grows with its draw count (about 2.3 µs a draw), and the GPU counters show vertex-only time at about 4 % occupancy. → [Mesh geometry draws gathered into one dispatch](../reference/shaders.md#mesh-geometry-draws-gathered-into-one-dispatch)
+- white blotches over Kokiri Forest's foliage, walkway and ground in Ocarina of Time, which are the house light tiles. The light-tile pass of task `a5288d0a6c4971fd` with meshes `e8c667282ba7bd9b` and `d4171cf9adf0504b` writes constant white through fragment `ea1bf96b72e72476`, and its triangles were corrupt. → [Mesh stage memory reserves the primitive index bytes for every primitive block](../reference/shaders.md#mesh-stage-memory-reserves-the-primitive-index-bytes-for-every-primitive-block)
+- a mesh shader's per-primitive outputs read as other values once it has more than 32 vertices: Ocarina of Time's Poe Sisters and Phantom Ganon paintings (mesh shaders `ee4ef51a4fddc28e` and `83c0dbc51c5481e3`, 128 vertices, 64 primitives, a per-primitive colour) came out solid green or magenta (pull request #1590). A mesh shader that draws points with a point size takes the size as its position's x. → [Mesh attributes: every vertex block before the primitive blocks](../reference/shaders.md#mesh-attributes-every-vertex-block-before-the-primitive-blocks)
+- a mesh-shaded draw shows nothing, though its workgroups run: every workgroup ends with a primitive count of 0. Once that is mended, a visibility buffer written from `[[primitive_id]]` holds only the index within the meshlet, and each pixel is shaded from the wrong cluster. → [Mesh shader per-primitive system values: the primitive count overwritten, the primitive id lost](../reference/shaders.md#mesh-shader-per-primitive-system-values-the-primitive-count-overwritten-the-primitive-id-lost)
+- thin streaks or stray triangles from a mesh shader over parts of the picture its geometry does not cover (PRAGMATA: white vertical streaks over the cockpit window in the opening). → [Mesh shaders that also address their vertices as records](../reference/shaders.md#mesh-shaders-that-also-address-their-vertices-as-records)
+- `NotSupportedException: Ampere 923 …: ISBERD mode f8 in a task or mesh shader` in the shader build; those mesh shaders are left out and their draws skipped (`[RED] DrawMeshTasks without its task and mesh shaders`). → [Mesh shaders that read their own outputs back](../reference/shaders.md#mesh-shaders-that-read-their-own-outputs-back)
+- a small scan or sort in a compute shader gives wrong results every frame, with no barrier in its loop (Orbitals: Niagara's sorted particle indices). → [Threadgroup stores in warp-synchronous code](../reference/shaders.md#threadgroup-stores-in-warp-synchronous-code)
+- `primitive type 14 not implemented`; patch draws skipped. → [Tessellation stages are not drawn](../reference/shaders.md#tessellation-stages-are-not-drawn)
+- a Switch 2 game's shaders do not translate (the translator reads Maxwell: 64-bit instructions behind scheduling words, a 0x50-byte SPH), or, rewritten as Maxwell code, UI text draws as solid boxes or not at all. → [Ampere shader code (Switch 2)](../reference/shaders.md#ampere-shader-code-switch-2)
+- a lit pass far slower on an M1 than the M4 Pro's figures suggest, the time spread over every material that loops over the scene's lights; dropping one material's draws (`DM_NVN_UB`) saved only its share. → [Storage words read one by one](../reference/shaders.md#storage-words-read-one-by-one)
+- `reflection conversion failed: B binding cp_i_cb3_0_ has no resolved slot number` at load, then `the dispatched program has no compute shader`; in the build, `SUATOM handle in bank 3` or `SURED handle in bank 3`, and bindings of an unrecognized kind for a typed buffer. Compute passes are skipped. → [Images and buffer textures with their handle in a uniform buffer](../reference/shaders.md#images-and-buffer-textures-with-their-handle-in-a-uniform-buffer)
+- a scene lit black with correct geometry. In `DM_NVN_PASSDUMP`, the lighting shader's bindings show `tex … tid=0 dummy` where the G-buffer should be, and a sampler bound where a texture is expected. → [Texture and sampler words in either order](../reference/shaders.md#texture-and-sampler-words-in-either-order)
