+## Game state
+
+- "stuck" at a screen with one draw per frame. → [Most draws are in command buffers replayed later](../reference/game-state.md#most-draws-are-in-command-buffers-replayed-later)
+- menus ignore A. → [Buttons mapped by position: B confirms](../reference/game-state.md#buttons-mapped-by-position-b-confirms)
+- a crash in `main+0x339c00` a second or two into the title, in love-nx's video module teardown (`love::video::theora::Video` → `~Worker`; its thread released the worker that the closing module deletes too). → [Any Lua error quits a LÖVE game](../reference/game-state.md#any-lua-error-quits-a-löve-game)
+- the TV latency calibration ("press A when you hear the fourth beat") ignores A. → [TV latency calibration's late, beat-timed listening window](../reference/game-state.md#tv-latency-calibrations-late-beat-timed-listening-window)
+- A at the title shows "Connecting to Battle.net", then "Failed to authenticate. Please try again."; OK goes back to the title, and every try ends the same way. No `[RED]` line. → ["Failed to authenticate" at the title: offline play only after a recent online login](../reference/game-state.md#failed-to-authenticate-at-the-title-offline-play-only-after-a-recent-online-login)
+- in a scripted run, a screen goes back by itself right after a confirm; the log shows `swkbd: … → no window, treated as cancel`. → [The software keyboard in scripted runs (`DM_KBD`)](../reference/game-state.md#the-software-keyboard-in-scripted-runs-dm_kbd)
+- a player join screen that ignores A (a character select with four "L + R to join" slots after the title). → [Player join screens (`hid::StartLrAssignmentMode`)](../reference/game-state.md#player-join-screens-hidstartlrassignmentmode)
