+DM_NVN_PREFETCH	switch	`0` turns off loading a program's shader libraries in the background when the game makes it (`nvnProgramSetShaders`); they load at its first draw instead
+DM_NVN_PRESENT_FINISH	diagnostic	`=1` makes each present return once the GPU has run the frame, so the game never runs ahead of the GPU
+DM_NVN_PROF	diagnostic	`=1` wraps the implemented NVN functions in a timing wrapper and collects the time each takes during recording
+DM_NVN_PROGTRACE	diagnostic	`=<vertex keys,...>` logs matching ProgramSetShaders calls and their guest backtraces
+DM_NVN_REGLUM	diagnostic	`=x0,y0,x1,y1:<file>` (normalized coordinates): on every present records the present number, time, mean luminance and a grayscale thumbnail of that region, to check animation speed against frame rate
+DM_NVN_REPORT_EXACT	switch	`0` refuses a partly covered uniform shadow over the whole 4 KB page of a counter report of a running submission, as before; by default only over the report's own 16 bytes, which the host writes when that submission completes
+DM_NVN_REUPLOADS	diagnostic	`=1` logs the first 400 re-uploads of textures taken from their storage: shape, size, how much was read from guest memory and how many images were copied from the texture it replaces, the frame and the submission, the pages written since the upload and where the first lies, and the GPU copies into it since then
+DM_NVN_RP_AREA	switch	`0` makes passes on targets of 16 M pixels or more cover the whole target, as before; by default a draw pass that loads what it keeps stops at the far corner of its scissor when that is at most half the target
